source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Read the folder and report what is wrong; writes nothing.

Usage: ink check [OPTIONS]

Also typed as ink c

Examples
  ink check           # Read this folder and list its problems
  ink check --strict  # The same, but a warning is an exit 6

Options
      --strict  Exit with 6 when there are warnings

Source
      --source <KIND>  `folder` reads the files on disk, `git` reads a commit
                       [default: `git` when .git exists, said as a notice]
      --rev <REV>      The commit to read, as `git rev-parse` takes it; only for
                       a git repository [default: HEAD]

Notes
  The folder is read and interpreted exactly as a build would; nothing is
  written.

Exit codes
  0  Done; warnings, if any, were printed
  1  The site has errors
  2  Wrong usage, or a folder that is missing; nothing was changed
  6  --strict was given and there were warnings

See also  ink build, ink explain
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
          (see `ink --help`)
